{"timestamp": "2026-02-04 19:41:56.108509", "event": "llm_start", "messages": "content=\"Based on the diagnosis report: ### Troubleshooting Diagnosis Report\\n\\n#### Network Overview:\\nThe network is an SDN star topology with one central switch (switch_0) and multiple edge switches (switch_1 to switch_8). Hosts (host_1 to host_8) are connected to edge switches, and all devices share a single access subnet (10.0.0.0/24). The management/control network (20.0.0.0/24) is used for OpenFlow communication with the SDN controller at 20.0.0.100.\\n\\n#### Reachability Analysis:\\nPing tests were conducted between hosts to assess connectivity and network health. Below are the findings:\\n\\n1. **Host-to-Host Connectivity**:\\n   - All hosts successfully communicated with each other.\\n   - No packet loss was observed in any of the tests (loss percentage = 0.0%).\\n   - RTT (Round-Trip Time) values varied across tests but remained within acceptable ranges:\\n     - Average RTT values ranged from approximately 44 ms to 52 ms.\\n     - Minimum RTT values were as low as 0.488 ms, while maximum RTT values reached up to 103.957 ms.\\n     - RTT standard deviation (mdev) values indicated some variability, but no extreme outliers were detected.\\n\\n2. **Latency Observations**:\\n   - The RTT values are slightly higher than expected for a local network, suggesting potential delays in the network path or processing overhead at switches.\\n   - The variability in RTT (mdev values) indicates inconsistent latency, which could be due to congestion or processing delays at the central switch (switch_0).\\n\\n#### Key Findings:\\n- **No Packet Loss**: All hosts successfully exchanged packets, indicating that the network is functional and there are no major connectivity issues.\\n- **Latency Variability**: The RTT values show some inconsistency, which may warrant further investigation into switch performance or network congestion.\\n- **Controller Communication**: While host-to-host communication is verified, the status of OpenFlow communication between switches and the SDN controller has not been assessed yet.\\n\\n#### Next Steps:\\nTo further diagnose the network:\\n1. Verify the OpenFlow connection status between switches and the SDN controller.\\n2. Investigate the central switch (switch_0) for potential congestion or processing delays.\\n3. Analyze traffic patterns and switch configurations to identify any bottlenecks.\\n\\nThis report provides an initial assessment of the network's health based on host reachability tests. Further analysis is required to ensure optimal performance and identify any underlying issues., please provide the submission. Do not submit if no report available.\" additional_kwargs={} response_metadata={} id='fbf1f3bc-4cbb-40c6-bee4-d0c9a1c1b041'", "model": {"lc": 1, "type": "constructor", "id": ["langchain", "chat_models", "openai", "ChatOpenAI"], "kwargs": {"model_name": "kt-gpt-oss-rh014", "temperature": 0.0, "openai_api_key": {"lc": 1, "type": "secret", "id": ["OPENAI_API_KEY"]}, "openai_api_base": "https://dev.kora.kt.co.kr/v2", "request_timeout": 180.0, "max_retries": 2}, "name": "ChatOpenAI"}}
